WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:32.641
<i>Previously on</i> Star Trek:
Strange New Worlds...

2
00:00:32.815 --> 00:00:33.990
<i>Six months nonstop.</i>

3
00:00:34.164 --> 00:00:35.209
<i>I'm just worried the crew</i>

4
00:00:35.383 --> 00:00:36.623
<i>is starting to feel the strain.</i>

5
00:00:36.688 --> 00:00:38.081
We could all use a night off.

6
00:00:38.255 --> 00:00:40.257
Why is everyone obsessed
with me taking breaks?

7
00:00:40.431 --> 00:00:42.129
Work will still be here in five minutes.

8
00:00:42.303 --> 00:00:44.392
Fine. Let's... relax.

9
00:00:44.653 --> 00:00:46.350
<i>My mind to your mind.</i>

10
00:00:46.524 --> 00:00:49.049
- You and I will remain friends.
- I think so. Spock.

11
00:00:49.223 --> 00:00:51.268
<i>Scotty acts like every time
I steer the ship.</i>

12
00:00:51.442 --> 00:00:53.836
<i>it makes his job harder. So he
added endless beeping...</i>

13
00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.162
<i>- to make my job harder.</i>
- There's a reason for those lights.

14
00:00:56.186 --> 00:00:57.622
Shut them off. Scotty.

15
00:00:57.796 --> 00:01:00.190
- Frickin' engineers.
- Bloody pilots.

16
00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:07.803
<i>Lieutenant Erica Ortegas personal log.</i>

17
00:01:08.024 --> 00:01:10.026
<i>Stardate 2011.7.</i>

18
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.897
<i>We're on our way
to the Rodaxian system.</i>

19
00:01:12.115 --> 00:01:13.875
<i>where the captain will be
negotiating a peace treaty</i>

20
00:01:13.899 --> 00:01:15.205
<i>in a civil war.</i>

21
00:01:16.728 --> 00:01:20.210
<i>And it's not exactly
an easy system to fly to.</i>

22
00:01:20.384 --> 00:01:23.561
<i>Which. thank goodness.
is why I'm at the helm.</i>

23
00:01:23.735 --> 00:01:26.086
<i>Lieutenant Montgomery Scott
personal log.</i>

24
00:01:26.347 --> 00:01:28.871
<i>Stardate 2011.7.</i>

25
00:01:29.045 --> 00:01:30.960
<i>As we head through
a fickle region of space.</i>

26
00:01:31.221 --> 00:01:33.101
<i>ship's been needing
round-the-clock maintenance.</i>

27
00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:35.530
<i>Normally I don't complain.
It's just that Beta</i>

28
00:01:35.704 --> 00:01:37.377
<i>and Gamma shifts
got shore leave last month.</i>

29
00:01:37.401 --> 00:01:39.273
<i>while Alpha shift didn't.</i>

30
00:01:39.447 --> 00:01:42.189
<i>Let's face it. Alpha shift's a big deal.</i>

31
00:01:42.363 --> 00:01:43.712
<i>But. come on. we need</i>

32
00:01:43.929 --> 00:01:45.757
<i>the same break Beta and Gamma get.</i>

33
00:01:45.931 --> 00:01:47.107
<i>It's wearing on everyone.</i>

34
00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:51.589
<i>The only reason this region of space</i>

35
00:01:51.763 --> 00:01:55.550
<i>is tricky is because of the way
some people choose to fly.</i>

36
00:01:55.724 --> 00:01:59.162
<i>And that's precisely why
I added the alert system.</i>

37
00:01:59.423 --> 00:02:00.859
<i>Going over my head</i>

38
00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.297
<i>to say I exceed parameters
was bad enough.</i>

39
00:02:03.471 --> 00:02:04.820
<i>Installing a warning light</i>

40
00:02:05.081 --> 00:02:06.822
<i>to tell me how to fly?</i>

41
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:08.606
<i>This feels personal.</i>

42
00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.391
<i>It's fine though. Everything's fine.</i>

43
00:02:10.565 --> 00:02:12.436
<i>Things get bumpy.
you push your way forward.</i>

44
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.525
<i>even if something's in your way.</i>

45
00:02:14.786 --> 00:02:16.745
<i>And she went over my head.</i>

46
00:02:16.919 --> 00:02:18.399
<i>Ignoring the controls.</i>

47
00:02:18.573 --> 00:02:20.140
<i>She-She's taking this too far.</i>

48
00:02:20.314 --> 00:02:22.881
<i>Someone's attitude
has everyone on edge.</i>

49
00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:24.666
<i>She's a know-it-all. arrogant...</i>

50
00:02:24.927 --> 00:02:26.450
<i>Micromanaging. rude...</i>

51
00:02:26.624 --> 00:02:28.844
<i>Constantly trying to take control...</i>

52
00:02:30.062 --> 00:02:31.760
- Lieutenant.
- Lieutenant.

53
00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:36.784
They look like they want
to kill each other.

54
00:02:36.808 --> 00:02:38.506
They're not the only ones.

55
00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.029
La'An is itching for a fight.

56
00:02:40.247 --> 00:02:41.927
which Spock is just trying to stay out of.

57
00:02:42.074 --> 00:02:45.817
Joseph needs to loosen up
even more than you do.

58
00:02:45.991 --> 00:02:47.210
Respectfully. sir.

59
00:02:47.471 --> 00:02:49.212
And don't get me started on Chapel

60
00:02:49.386 --> 00:02:51.127
and whatever's going on there.

61
00:02:52.389 --> 00:02:53.825
Damn it.

62
00:02:54.913 --> 00:02:57.264
I guess I have just been
thinking about negotiations.

63
00:02:57.525 --> 00:02:59.744
Which I'm going to need
Alpha shift's help with.

64
00:02:59.918 --> 00:03:02.094
And they very much need a break.

65
00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:04.271
Suggestions?

66
00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:08.230
<i>Hey!</i>

67
00:03:08.318 --> 00:03:10.190
<i>I didn't see you there.</i>

68
00:03:10.364 --> 00:03:11.930
<i>Just kidding. I did.</i>

69
00:03:12.104 --> 00:03:14.672
<i>Are you ready for the time of your life?</i>

70
00:03:14.846 --> 00:03:17.284
<i>Because I'm here to give that to you.</i>

71
00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:21.636
<i>"Dendru's the name. or you can
call me "your new best friend</i>

72
00:03:21.897 --> 00:03:24.291
<i>on your personal journey
to de-stresstation."</i>

73
00:03:24.465 --> 00:03:25.770
<i>And this...</i>

74
00:03:26.031 --> 00:03:28.164
<i>is the Cesnar Grand.</i>

75
00:03:28.338 --> 00:03:30.558
<i>Thanks to our planet's</i>

76
00:03:30.732 --> 00:03:33.691
<i>one-of-a-kind intoxicating atmosphere.</i>

77
00:03:33.865 --> 00:03:37.782
<i>each visitor experiences a one-of-a-kind.</i>

78
00:03:38.043 --> 00:03:39.436
<i>customized journey</i>

79
00:03:39.654 --> 00:03:42.787
<i>that will provide exactly what they need</i>

80
00:03:42.961 --> 00:03:44.006
<i>to relax.</i>

81
00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:47.183
<i>Speaking of relaxing...</i>

82
00:03:49.272 --> 00:03:52.057
<i>This is a place to say
"no way" to those icky parts</i>

83
00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:55.147
<i>of your daily life. Even technology!</i>

84
00:03:55.322 --> 00:03:57.411
<i>That's right. This is a tech-free zone.</i>

85
00:03:57.585 --> 00:04:00.805
<i>The only focus here
is living your best life!</i>

86
00:04:00.979 --> 00:04:02.546
<i>Atmospheric effects harmlessly wear off</i>

87
00:04:02.851 --> 00:04:04.698
<i>shortly after departure.
Arrival on the planet is</i>

88
00:04:04.722 --> 00:04:06.657
<i>an explicit release
of all liabilities on the part</i>

89
00:04:06.681 --> 00:04:08.001
<i>of Cesnar Grand or its employees.</i>

90
00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.816
Alpha crew is taking shore leave.

91
00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:13.890
And the Rodaxian peace talks?

92
00:04:13.992 --> 00:04:15.272
We have two weeks before we land

93
00:04:15.385 --> 00:04:16.604
in their region.

94
00:04:16.821 --> 00:04:18.146
And the resort planet's directly
on our path.

95
00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:19.650
Nothing against vacations.

96
00:04:19.824 --> 00:04:21.696
but the Rodaxians are very specific

97
00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:23.437
in how they like to be spoken to.

98
00:04:23.611 --> 00:04:25.352
I was hoping we would use this time

99
00:04:25.526 --> 00:04:26.966
to review the formal kickoff speech.

100
00:04:27.223 --> 00:04:28.863
And I was worried
about having enough time

101
00:04:29.007 --> 00:04:31.140
to do all the ship repairs
before negotiations. too.

102
00:04:31.314 --> 00:04:33.751
A pit stop sounds great to me.

103
00:04:33.925 --> 00:04:35.144
A break is crucial to take

104
00:04:35.405 --> 00:04:37.146
the edge off before the negotiations.

105
00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.200
A day or two on Cesnar
and you'll all still have

106
00:04:39.235 --> 00:04:40.275
a week to work after that.

107
00:04:40.454 --> 00:04:41.585
The spokesperson said

108
00:04:41.759 --> 00:04:43.152
"intoxicating atmosphere."

109
00:04:43.413 --> 00:04:44.762
- Is it safe?
- Completely.

110
00:04:44.936 --> 00:04:46.895
Anyone who goes
will feel naturally inebriated

111
00:04:47.069 --> 00:04:48.288
by the planetary gases.

112
00:04:48.592 --> 00:04:50.377
The effect is different for each person.

113
00:04:50.551 --> 00:04:53.641
and it wears off. like.
an hour after leaving.

114
00:04:53.902 --> 00:04:55.730
I promise you.

115
00:04:55.904 --> 00:04:58.733
this will be the best shore leave ever.

116
00:04:58.907 --> 00:05:00.517
Can't argue with that.

117
00:05:09.396 --> 00:05:12.224
<i>Do you think we can survive
a week without our tricorders?</i>

118
00:05:12.486 --> 00:05:16.490
<i>They didn't say this place
was mandatory tech-free.</i>

119
00:05:16.664 --> 00:05:17.926
I'll still get some work in.

120
00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.058
I brought one as well.

121
00:05:21.103 --> 00:05:22.757
You know. it's a thin atmosphere.

122
00:05:22.931 --> 00:05:24.778
- You need to let up on the.
- On the backseat driving?

123
00:05:24.802 --> 00:05:26.413
Is that what you were gonna say?

124
00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.347
I was gonna say if you come in
hot. you're gonna land hard.

125
00:05:28.371 --> 00:05:30.417
I'm setting down
on a shuttle storage conveyer.

126
00:05:30.591 --> 00:05:31.853
Pretty much parks itself.

127
00:05:32.114 --> 00:05:33.637
Right. But you still need to brake.

128
00:05:33.811 --> 00:05:35.509
Whoa!

129
00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.207
Great. Now I'll have to stay and fix that.

130
00:05:38.381 --> 00:05:40.165
Well. that would be a tragedy.

131
00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.660
What. did you do that on purpose?

132
00:05:41.732 --> 00:05:43.299
I didn't.

133
00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:44.885
But if you're thinking
this place better be big enough

134
00:05:44.909 --> 00:05:46.060
for us to get a break from each other.

135
00:05:46.084 --> 00:05:47.216
I am right there with you.

136
00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:48.870
Christine. how long

137
00:05:49.087 --> 00:05:51.916
until that atmospheric
inebriation kicks in?

138
00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:53.657
As soon as that door opens.

139
00:05:53.831 --> 00:05:55.659
just count down from ten.

140
00:05:58.967 --> 00:05:59.967
Ten.

141
00:06:00.055 --> 00:06:01.491
Nine.

142
00:06:01.665 --> 00:06:02.665
Eight.

143
00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.190
Seven. Six.

144
00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:06.670
- Four.
- Seven.

145
00:06:06.844 --> 00:06:08.759
- Five.
- Six.

146
00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:10.195
Four.

147
00:06:10.457 --> 00:06:11.457
Three.

148
00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.156
Four and a half!

149
00:06:55.806 --> 00:06:57.199
Lieutenant!

150
00:06:57.373 --> 00:07:00.550
What are you...

151
00:07:00.724 --> 00:07:02.324
I don't know! I don't remember anything!

152
00:07:02.465 --> 00:07:04.336
Am I a mugato now?

153
00:07:04.511 --> 00:07:06.643
What's the last thing you remember?

154
00:07:06.904 --> 00:07:07.905
Shuttle.

155
00:07:08.079 --> 00:07:09.994
You biffed the landing.

156
00:07:10.168 --> 00:07:11.648
Are you drunk?

157
00:07:11.909 --> 00:07:13.041
Why am I not drunk?

158
00:07:15.347 --> 00:07:16.436
Can you just...

159
00:07:17.654 --> 00:07:18.873
Sit down.

160
00:07:19.047 --> 00:07:19.874
On the floor.

161
00:07:20.048 --> 00:07:21.876
Don't touch anything.

162
00:07:24.879 --> 00:07:27.185
So bossy.

163
00:07:28.099 --> 00:07:29.710
Hello! Me again.

164
00:07:29.884 --> 00:07:32.495
- Again?
- A message came for your captain.

165
00:07:32.756 --> 00:07:34.476
It's time-sensitive. He wasn't in his room.

166
00:07:34.628 --> 00:07:36.804
so I am hoping
that you can deliver it to him.

167
00:07:37.065 --> 00:07:38.109
Can you do that?

168
00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:39.459
Hey. man.

169
00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:40.720
I'm confused.

170
00:07:40.895 --> 00:07:43.027
- Go on.
- Promises were made.

171
00:07:43.201 --> 00:07:45.377
and none of those promises
included a hangover

172
00:07:45.552 --> 00:07:47.641
or missing time.

173
00:07:47.815 --> 00:07:50.644
Sometimes if you're hanging on
to negative emotions.

174
00:07:50.818 --> 00:07:54.125
it can negate or alter
the effects of the atmosphere.

175
00:07:54.299 --> 00:07:55.779
That wasn't in the brochure.

176
00:07:55.953 --> 00:07:57.825
It was. it was. It was in the fine print.

177
00:07:57.999 --> 00:07:59.740
Well. actually. it was in the micro print.

178
00:07:59.914 --> 00:08:01.282
But the fine print clearly directs you

179
00:08:01.306 --> 00:08:02.656
to read the micro print.

180
00:08:02.917 --> 00:08:03.937
So. really. it's all quite legally binding.

181
00:08:03.961 --> 00:08:04.961
Tell you what.

182
00:08:05.136 --> 00:08:05.963
after you deliver that.

183
00:08:06.137 --> 00:08:07.312
I promise to fix you up.

184
00:08:07.487 --> 00:08:08.531
And in the meantime.

185
00:08:08.836 --> 00:08:10.490
just remember. take deep breaths.

186
00:08:10.664 --> 00:08:12.404
Deep breaths. And. you know.

187
00:08:12.579 --> 00:08:14.755
the-the deposit is nonrefundable.

188
00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:16.974
- What is that?
- A letter.

189
00:08:17.148 --> 00:08:18.410
A piece of paper?

190
00:08:18.672 --> 00:08:19.736
Don't you remember the video?

191
00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.370
This is a tech-free zone.

192
00:08:21.544 --> 00:08:22.632
Hence...

193
00:08:25.461 --> 00:08:26.549
You stay here.

194
00:08:26.723 --> 00:08:27.724
Or not.

195
00:08:27.898 --> 00:08:30.771
Or do whatever you're gonna do.

196
00:08:32.381 --> 00:08:33.817
Souvenir.

197
00:08:33.991 --> 00:08:36.733
- It's sharp.
- Or you can't be left alone.

198
00:08:36.907 --> 00:08:38.343
Of course.

199
00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:40.930
We'll just deliver this note to the captain.

200
00:08:40.955 --> 00:08:41.955
and he can deal with you.

201
00:08:41.999 --> 00:08:43.348
'Cause there's no way

202
00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:45.443
we're gonna be stuck
with each other on vacation.

203
00:08:52.749 --> 00:08:54.446
<i>Space.</i>

204
00:08:55.317 --> 00:08:57.841
<i>The final frontier.</i>

205
00:08:59.539 --> 00:09:03.281
<i>These are the voyages
of the starship</i> Enterprise.

206
00:09:05.501 --> 00:09:07.111
<i>Its five-year mission:</i>

207
00:09:07.285 --> 00:09:10.419
<i>to explore strange new worlds...</i>

208
00:09:12.595 --> 00:09:14.858
<i>to seek out new life</i>

209
00:09:15.032 --> 00:09:17.557
<i>and new civilizations...</i>

210
00:09:18.558 --> 00:09:22.605
<i>to boldly go
where no one has gone before.</i>

211
00:10:39.682 --> 00:10:42.729
Guess I'll just start at door number one.

212
00:10:42.903 --> 00:10:45.166
Someone has to know
where the captain is.

213
00:10:48.212 --> 00:10:49.736
Stop.

214
00:10:55.655 --> 00:10:58.005
Are you Lieutenant Ortegas
and Lieutenant Scott?

215
00:10:58.179 --> 00:10:59.920
Boy.

216
00:11:08.363 --> 00:11:09.712
I apologize for the mess.

217
00:11:10.017 --> 00:11:11.937
- Is Captain Pike here?
- Not that I am aware of.

218
00:11:12.062 --> 00:11:14.606
- Where's La'An?
- She is on a more spirited journey than my own.

219
00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:17.154
As you can no doubt see.
I am quite incapacitated.

220
00:11:17.415 --> 00:11:18.721
- You are?
- Entirely.

221
00:11:18.895 --> 00:11:20.331
You seem pretty normal.

222
00:11:20.505 --> 00:11:23.683
Do you see James Kirk in this room?

223
00:11:23.857 --> 00:11:25.641
No...

224
00:11:25.902 --> 00:11:27.382
Unless he's invisible.

225
00:11:27.556 --> 00:11:29.340
Cloaked.

226
00:11:29.514 --> 00:11:31.821
I have been hallucinating
a manifestation of James Kirk.

227
00:11:31.995 --> 00:11:33.235
We've been playing board games.

228
00:11:33.475 --> 00:11:35.216
Wonder what that's all about.

229
00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:36.846
This is fun and all. but do
you know where the captain is?

230
00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:38.088
I need to find him now.

231
00:11:38.306 --> 00:11:39.829
- You appear tense.
- I don't remember

232
00:11:40.047 --> 00:11:41.851
what I did last night.
I have a pounding headache.

233
00:11:41.875 --> 00:11:43.790
And if I want to get
any enjoyment at all out of

234
00:11:43.964 --> 00:11:46.044
this so-called vacation.
I apparently need to deliver

235
00:11:46.096 --> 00:11:48.055
a note to him first. So. yeah.

236
00:11:48.229 --> 00:11:49.317
tense.

237
00:11:49.665 --> 00:11:50.903
You do not recall fighting a dragon?

238
00:11:50.927 --> 00:11:52.189
Is that a joke?

239
00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:53.906
I heard you shouting
in the corridor that you

240
00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:55.192
"got the dragon."

241
00:11:55.627 --> 00:11:57.934
I'll add that to my list
of things to figure out.

242
00:11:58.108 --> 00:11:59.108
And Pike is...?

243
00:11:59.196 --> 00:12:00.328
He mentioned Uhura's party.

244
00:12:00.502 --> 00:12:01.329
Two doors south.

245
00:12:01.503 --> 00:12:02.852
Well. there we go.

246
00:12:03.026 --> 00:12:04.071
An actual lead.

247
00:12:04.245 --> 00:12:06.203
Thank you.

248
00:12:11.905 --> 00:12:14.821
Should we order some fries?

249
00:12:15.604 --> 00:12:18.302
Do you think my seeing you here
has deeper meaning?

250
00:12:18.476 --> 00:12:20.174
Deeper than what?

251
00:12:20.435 --> 00:12:23.743
Perhaps a remnant of you was
left behind after our mind meld

252
00:12:23.917 --> 00:12:27.790
and is now filling an emotional void.

253
00:12:27.964 --> 00:12:30.097
Do you need a hug?

254
00:12:30.271 --> 00:12:33.230
Bring it in here.

255
00:12:36.668 --> 00:12:38.105
Don't even think about it.

256
00:12:41.108 --> 00:12:43.371
My friends.

257
00:12:43.632 --> 00:12:44.632
You're here.

258
00:12:44.676 --> 00:12:48.419
Erica. you were so right.

259
00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:51.205
Relaxation is just so...

260
00:12:51.379 --> 00:12:53.468
relaxing.

261
00:12:53.642 --> 00:12:54.904
I love it. Boop.

262
00:12:56.297 --> 00:12:58.299
This is amazing.

263
00:12:58.473 --> 00:13:00.431
This <i>is</i> amazing.

264
00:13:00.605 --> 00:13:02.445
- Is Pike here?
- I have to give him something.

265
00:13:02.694 --> 00:13:04.609
Then I need to stay here
and never leave.

266
00:13:05.915 --> 00:13:07.090
Yeah.

267
00:13:07.961 --> 00:13:09.353
No.

268
00:13:09.527 --> 00:13:11.268
- He's not here.
- Do you know where he is?

269
00:13:11.442 --> 00:13:13.793
It's not my journey to know.

270
00:13:13.967 --> 00:13:16.099
We're all on our own journeys here.

271
00:13:16.273 --> 00:13:18.754
Why would my journey
involve breaking my arm

272
00:13:19.015 --> 00:13:20.451
and maybe a dragon?

273
00:13:20.625 --> 00:13:22.802
Chapel mentioned your cast.

274
00:13:23.063 --> 00:13:24.503
Said you didn't want your arm fixed.

275
00:13:24.542 --> 00:13:26.153
Glutton for pain.

276
00:13:26.327 --> 00:13:28.329
Probably where
all that anger comes from.

277
00:13:28.503 --> 00:13:29.503
I'm not angry.

278
00:13:29.721 --> 00:13:31.506
- Okay.
- You know what?

279
00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:32.681
You stay with Uhura.

280
00:13:32.855 --> 00:13:33.856
I'll find Pike.

281
00:13:35.597 --> 00:13:37.686
No. you guys are...

282
00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.907
That is so not my vibe right now. But...

283
00:13:41.168 --> 00:13:42.343
good luck on your journey.

284
00:13:43.953 --> 00:13:45.433
Can you at least give me something?

285
00:13:45.607 --> 00:13:47.565
- Any idea where Pike might be?
- He...

286
00:13:47.739 --> 00:13:50.090
is... on... his... own...

287
00:13:50.351 --> 00:13:51.351
journey.

288
00:13:54.398 --> 00:13:56.661
Bye. Bring back cookies.

289
00:13:56.836 --> 00:13:59.142
Her hands are so soft.

290
00:14:05.235 --> 00:14:07.324
Scotty.

291
00:14:07.498 --> 00:14:09.587
Scotty. Scotty.

292
00:14:09.761 --> 00:14:13.156
You can't go off on your own.

293
00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:16.116
Since apparently another task I have

294
00:14:16.377 --> 00:14:18.161
is babysitting a small grown man.

295
00:14:18.335 --> 00:14:19.728
I am average-sized.

296
00:14:19.946 --> 00:14:22.122
I'm just following the clues. okay?

297
00:14:22.296 --> 00:14:23.882
- Really want to win the big prize.
- There is no prize.

298
00:14:23.906 --> 00:14:25.473
We're delivering a note to the captain.

299
00:14:25.734 --> 00:14:27.475
It's not a scavenger hunt.

300
00:14:54.371 --> 00:14:56.460
She's pretty good.

301
00:14:56.634 --> 00:14:58.767
She probably knows where Pike is.

302
00:15:00.029 --> 00:15:02.989
How are there
so many Klingon power ballads?

303
00:15:03.163 --> 00:15:05.774
And she signed up to sing 15 in a row.

304
00:15:05.948 --> 00:15:08.037
Warrior's songs.

305
00:15:08.995 --> 00:15:09.995
Friends.

306
00:15:10.039 --> 00:15:11.040
- Doctor.
- Showtime!

307
00:15:11.214 --> 00:15:12.215
Have you.

308
00:15:16.263 --> 00:15:18.874
Have you seen Captain Pike?!

309
00:15:20.745 --> 00:15:22.245
I'll take one of whatever
that is you're making.

310
00:15:22.269 --> 00:15:23.531
No. No. No. he won't.

311
00:15:23.705 --> 00:15:26.577
And you don't work here. Doctor.

312
00:15:26.751 --> 00:15:28.101
What is it?

313
00:15:28.275 --> 00:15:29.841
It's green.

314
00:15:30.016 --> 00:15:31.321
Cool. right?

315
00:15:31.582 --> 00:15:32.888
How did you learn to do that?

316
00:15:33.062 --> 00:15:34.629
I'm just winging it.

317
00:15:34.803 --> 00:15:36.587
When I move my hands.
I'm usually worried

318
00:15:36.761 --> 00:15:38.328
about people's lives.

319
00:15:38.502 --> 00:15:39.634
But now?

320
00:15:41.592 --> 00:15:43.464
It's like Una singing.

321
00:15:48.904 --> 00:15:50.253
That's cool. man.

322
00:15:53.256 --> 00:15:54.692
Wait. Doctor.

323
00:15:54.866 --> 00:15:57.478
The captain.

324
00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:07.400
Captain?

325
00:16:09.969 --> 00:16:10.969
Hi.

326
00:16:11.013 --> 00:16:12.754
Can I ask you a question?

327
00:16:12.928 --> 00:16:14.451
What would you think of a face tattoo?

328
00:16:14.625 --> 00:16:16.149
You should get one. Mr. Scott.

329
00:16:16.323 --> 00:16:17.498
You'd look good.

330
00:16:17.759 --> 00:16:19.041
Well. I don't tell this to everyone.

331
00:16:19.065 --> 00:16:20.370
but I actually have a tattoo.

332
00:16:20.544 --> 00:16:21.544
On my - Stop.

333
00:16:21.589 --> 00:16:24.070
Sir. a message came for you.

334
00:16:24.244 --> 00:16:25.027
Thank you.

335
00:16:25.201 --> 00:16:26.333
You shouldn't do it.

336
00:16:26.507 --> 00:16:27.507
Old-school.

337
00:16:27.638 --> 00:16:28.770
Paper envelope. I like it.

338
00:16:28.944 --> 00:16:30.467
We should get these for the ship.

339
00:16:30.728 --> 00:16:34.036
Drive Uhura crazy.

340
00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:36.343
So. apparently.

341
00:16:36.517 --> 00:16:38.954
the Rodaxian diplomats

342
00:16:39.128 --> 00:16:41.000
are coming to us.

343
00:16:41.174 --> 00:16:42.610
That's good.

344
00:16:42.871 --> 00:16:46.135
And they'll be here in approximately

345
00:16:46.309 --> 00:16:47.832
two hours.

346
00:16:48.007 --> 00:16:50.879
We're not meeting them for two weeks.

347
00:16:52.924 --> 00:16:53.969
No.

348
00:16:54.143 --> 00:16:56.145
What should we do?

349
00:16:56.319 --> 00:16:57.581
You...

350
00:16:57.755 --> 00:16:59.105
go get the shuttle.

351
00:16:59.279 --> 00:17:01.194
And then by the time you come back.

352
00:17:01.368 --> 00:17:03.196
I'll be done
with the horsey thingy on my arm

353
00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:06.329
and then I'll have everybody rounded up

354
00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:08.679
and ready to go. partner.

355
00:17:08.853 --> 00:17:10.594
Scotty. stay here.

356
00:17:10.768 --> 00:17:11.919
And let you biff the shuttle again?

357
00:17:11.943 --> 00:17:13.119
Hey. hey. hey.

358
00:17:13.293 --> 00:17:15.643
I like you two having fun together.

359
00:17:15.904 --> 00:17:17.471
You should keep it going.

360
00:17:21.997 --> 00:17:23.868
You're gonna have to work fast.

361
00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.784
You should come to Montana.

362
00:17:28.525 --> 00:17:31.093
This is the worst vacation ever.

363
00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:35.402
Let's do that one. Tellurite.

364
00:17:35.576 --> 00:17:38.318
- Sexy.
- We can't just take...

365
00:17:38.579 --> 00:17:40.363
Hang on.

366
00:17:44.106 --> 00:17:46.065
Our shuttle's supposed to be right here.

367
00:17:46.326 --> 00:17:48.110
- Did you move it?
- Why would I move it?

368
00:17:48.284 --> 00:17:50.634
I don't know. Why did you
install warning lights?

369
00:17:50.808 --> 00:17:53.128
No one could move it without
the duotronic processing chip.

370
00:17:53.289 --> 00:17:54.943
We gave that to...

371
00:17:55.117 --> 00:17:56.988
an attendant. right?
I kind of remember that.

372
00:17:57.163 --> 00:17:58.251
Do you have it now?

373
00:18:00.905 --> 00:18:02.777
Look. whoever has that moved it.

374
00:18:04.257 --> 00:18:05.867
Hi.

375
00:18:06.128 --> 00:18:07.260
Hey.

376
00:18:07.608 --> 00:18:09.566
Do you know
what happened to our shuttle?

377
00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:11.394
Boxy. Beige-white.

378
00:18:11.568 --> 00:18:12.743
Federation issue.

379
00:18:12.917 --> 00:18:15.094
- I gave the chip to him.
- Me?

380
00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:18.575
A few hours ago.

381
00:18:20.142 --> 00:18:23.580
"Whoever has that moved it."

382
00:18:23.841 --> 00:18:24.842
Where'd you put it?

383
00:18:25.016 --> 00:18:26.124
I don't think I would've taken it.

384
00:18:26.148 --> 00:18:28.759
That doesn't sound like...

385
00:18:28.933 --> 00:18:30.587
I don't remember doing that.

386
00:18:30.761 --> 00:18:31.893
So what now?

387
00:18:32.154 --> 00:18:33.982
We're screwed.

388
00:18:36.506 --> 00:18:38.813
Yeah. that's bad.

389
00:18:45.211 --> 00:18:46.411
The shuttle could be anywhere.

390
00:18:46.603 --> 00:18:48.043
I was thinking maybe it was cloaked.

391
00:18:48.127 --> 00:18:49.127
- Like Kirk.
- Okay.

392
00:18:49.171 --> 00:18:50.433
I tried to be cool to you.

393
00:18:50.607 --> 00:18:52.261
What does you uncool
to someone look like?

394
00:18:52.435 --> 00:18:54.457
But now my vacation is ruined.
the shuttle is missing.

395
00:18:54.481 --> 00:18:57.179
and the peace talks are blown.
thanks to you.

396
00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.026
You're acting like
there's no way to find it.

397
00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:00.356
It's still somewhere.

398
00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:01.966
We just need...

399
00:19:02.228 --> 00:19:03.751
My tricorder.

400
00:19:03.925 --> 00:19:06.057
We could use that as a locator.

401
00:19:06.232 --> 00:19:08.384
Wait. that's somehow actually
a great idea. Where is it?

402
00:19:08.408 --> 00:19:09.583
I left it on the shuttle.

403
00:19:11.454 --> 00:19:13.108
But I do know one person

404
00:19:13.282 --> 00:19:16.329
who would never leave
a tricorder behind.

405
00:19:16.981 --> 00:19:18.766
I'm not giving you my tricorder.

406
00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:19.984
Why not?

407
00:19:20.159 --> 00:19:23.553
Because giving you <i>my</i> tricorder

408
00:19:23.727 --> 00:19:25.512
is not my journey.

409
00:19:25.686 --> 00:19:26.924
You need to follow your journey.

410
00:19:26.948 --> 00:19:28.776
Wait. what if your journey

411
00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:30.778
is our journey?

412
00:19:30.952 --> 00:19:32.214
Ours...

413
00:19:32.432 --> 00:19:34.042
Lieutenant Ortegas and I. that is

414
00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:37.350
is to track down a shuttle
together using your tricorder.

415
00:19:37.524 --> 00:19:39.482
Okay.

416
00:19:39.656 --> 00:19:41.092
You two working together.

417
00:19:41.267 --> 00:19:43.138
That does feel like your journey.

418
00:19:43.312 --> 00:19:45.575
Yep. That's our journey. Tricorder.

419
00:19:45.836 --> 00:19:46.924
Before I give it to you.

420
00:19:47.098 --> 00:19:50.580
you two need to clear this energy.

421
00:19:50.841 --> 00:19:51.668
Apologize to each other.

422
00:19:51.842 --> 00:19:52.887
Apologize for what?

423
00:19:53.061 --> 00:19:54.061
Let's just do it.

424
00:19:54.105 --> 00:19:55.585
Erica.

425
00:19:55.759 --> 00:19:58.284
I'm sorry that I...

426
00:19:59.807 --> 00:20:00.895
doubted you.

427
00:20:01.156 --> 00:20:03.027
- And your turn.
- Okay.

428
00:20:03.289 --> 00:20:04.507
And. Monty. I

429
00:20:04.681 --> 00:20:06.335
Montgomery. Hate that.

430
00:20:06.509 --> 00:20:08.163
I'm sorry...

431
00:20:08.337 --> 00:20:10.078
I was upset

432
00:20:10.252 --> 00:20:13.124
about your constant doubting of me.

433
00:20:14.996 --> 00:20:16.389
There.

434
00:20:16.563 --> 00:20:18.129
Don't we all feel so much better?

435
00:20:18.304 --> 00:20:19.304
- Great.
- Yep.

436
00:20:21.916 --> 00:20:24.527
Come back soon! You know you want to!

437
00:20:24.701 --> 00:20:27.008
Who wants a shot?!

438
00:20:27.182 --> 00:20:28.183
I got this.

439
00:20:28.357 --> 00:20:29.619
It's my job. Whoa!

440
00:20:29.793 --> 00:20:31.708
Bright.

441
00:20:31.882 --> 00:20:33.362
I can see the shuttle

442
00:20:33.536 --> 00:20:34.861
through the hotel security system.

443
00:20:34.885 --> 00:20:35.930
Here. look.

444
00:20:36.191 --> 00:20:37.366
Where'd you go?

445
00:20:37.584 --> 00:20:39.150
There you are.

446
00:20:39.325 --> 00:20:40.500
What the hell?

447
00:20:43.677 --> 00:20:45.418
It was a security system.

448
00:20:45.592 --> 00:20:47.091
Why would you throw it at me
to show me

449
00:20:47.115 --> 00:20:48.515
- a security system?
- I don't know.

450
00:20:48.899 --> 00:20:51.162
I'm probably not the best
decision-maker right now.

451
00:20:51.337 --> 00:20:53.904
- Understatement.
- Therefore this might not be the best plan.

452
00:20:54.078 --> 00:20:56.907
The security network had
a hub in the central office.

453
00:20:57.081 --> 00:20:59.388
So we go there. hack into the computer.

454
00:20:59.562 --> 00:21:00.955
track our shuttle. Boom.

455
00:21:01.216 --> 00:21:02.609
Yepper yep.

456
00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:04.219
Exactly.

457
00:21:04.393 --> 00:21:07.004
Can you hack into a computer right now?

458
00:21:07.178 --> 00:21:09.093
Probably no.

459
00:21:09.355 --> 00:21:10.660
Not a chance. no.

460
00:21:10.921 --> 00:21:12.358
Then we'll get someone who can.

461
00:21:13.489 --> 00:21:14.621
I may not be very useful.

462
00:21:14.795 --> 00:21:17.014
given my clearly inebriated state.

463
00:21:17.276 --> 00:21:19.060
You know you seem totally fine.

464
00:21:19.234 --> 00:21:20.496
Absurd.

465
00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:21.976
Are you sure you saw a computer?

466
00:21:22.150 --> 00:21:23.150
Because I don't see one.

467
00:21:23.282 --> 00:21:25.066
Yeah. I'm positive.

468
00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:26.459
I think.

469
00:21:30.071 --> 00:21:31.420
It is coming from this.

470
00:21:31.594 --> 00:21:33.596
That is a plant.

471
00:21:35.381 --> 00:21:37.208
I believe this is
photosynthetic technology.

472
00:21:37.383 --> 00:21:38.949
I assumed that was only theoretical.

473
00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:41.343
It's a plant.

474
00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:43.650
Perhaps I can telepathically link.

475
00:21:43.824 --> 00:21:47.001
What. read the plant's plant mind?

476
00:21:58.665 --> 00:22:01.189
My mind to your leaves.

477
00:22:01.363 --> 00:22:04.105
My thoughts to your root system.

478
00:22:06.542 --> 00:22:08.065
I can see the security map.

479
00:22:08.239 --> 00:22:10.329
The shuttle is just north.

480
00:22:11.286 --> 00:22:13.723
An area run by a local gang of thieves.

481
00:22:13.984 --> 00:22:16.378
I would recommend
bringing La'An as muscle.

482
00:22:16.639 --> 00:22:18.728
She has quite a bit
of pent-up energy today.

483
00:22:18.989 --> 00:22:20.339
So she's even scarier?

484
00:22:20.600 --> 00:22:23.646
She is much. much scarier.

485
00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:25.996
The three of us will be fine.

486
00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:27.389
I should not join you.

487
00:22:27.563 --> 00:22:30.392
This is pretty important. Spock.

488
00:22:32.525 --> 00:22:35.310
Are you both plants right now?

489
00:22:35.484 --> 00:22:37.312
No.

490
00:22:37.486 --> 00:22:39.575
I should rest.

491
00:22:41.316 --> 00:22:42.356
I mean. maybe I'm a plant.

492
00:22:42.491 --> 00:22:43.492
You're not a plant.

493
00:22:43.666 --> 00:22:45.233
Let's get La'An.

494
00:22:48.367 --> 00:22:51.631
Photosynthetic technology?

495
00:22:51.805 --> 00:22:52.849
Nice.

496
00:22:53.197 --> 00:22:55.374
I may know why I am imagining you.

497
00:22:56.766 --> 00:22:59.987
I've never had what humans
call a "human best friend."

498
00:23:00.161 --> 00:23:05.514
We don't actually call it
a <i>human</i> best friend.

499
00:23:05.688 --> 00:23:09.562
But I think you mean someone
that you can be vulnerable with.

500
00:23:09.736 --> 00:23:12.739
I have many things I want to talk about.

501
00:23:13.609 --> 00:23:14.654
Fears.

502
00:23:14.828 --> 00:23:15.828
hopes.

503
00:23:15.959 --> 00:23:17.352
dreams.

504
00:23:17.744 --> 00:23:19.789
I believe you are here
so I can share them with you.

505
00:23:19.963 --> 00:23:23.184
Even though you are in fact not here.

506
00:23:24.446 --> 00:23:25.926
Okay. buddy.

507
00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:28.407
Let's talk.

508
00:23:29.408 --> 00:23:31.018
Weapons are not necessary.

509
00:23:31.192 --> 00:23:33.847
This is a relaxation class.

510
00:23:34.021 --> 00:23:35.239
Was!

511
00:23:35.457 --> 00:23:37.590
Now it's an Anbo-jyutsu tournament

512
00:23:37.764 --> 00:23:38.852
to the death!

513
00:23:39.113 --> 00:23:40.113
Everyone form factions!

514
00:23:40.244 --> 00:23:41.855
Now! Stand up.

515
00:23:42.072 --> 00:23:43.833
- On your feet. On your feet.
- Yeah. I'd bet on the left team.

516
00:23:43.857 --> 00:23:45.511
- Sturdier.
- Feet together.

517
00:23:45.685 --> 00:23:47.165
- Stand up tall.
- I'm grabbing La'An.

518
00:23:47.251 --> 00:23:48.731
You. over there.

519
00:23:48.905 --> 00:23:49.993
Get in line.

520
00:23:50.429 --> 00:23:52.126
- You want some. too?
- No.

521
00:23:52.300 --> 00:23:53.344
Do you?

522
00:23:53.519 --> 00:23:54.563
- Do you?
- Definitely not.

523
00:23:54.737 --> 00:23:58.088
But I do have just the job for you.

524
00:23:58.262 --> 00:23:59.699
Bring the stick.

525
00:24:06.314 --> 00:24:07.924
Okay. so we'll go in.

526
00:24:08.098 --> 00:24:10.100
make some threats. get our shuttle back.

527
00:24:10.274 --> 00:24:11.362
He must be in charge.

528
00:24:11.537 --> 00:24:12.929
Stay here.

529
00:24:13.103 --> 00:24:15.845
I threaten best alone.

530
00:24:17.238 --> 00:24:21.198
Hey! You. seen
a Federation ship around here?

531
00:24:21.460 --> 00:24:23.200
Seems like it's going well.

532
00:24:28.902 --> 00:24:31.557
Still might be going well.

533
00:24:31.731 --> 00:24:33.689
We don't know what he's into.

534
00:24:33.863 --> 00:24:35.561
Maybe he likes that.

535
00:24:38.433 --> 00:24:40.261
He tell you where it is?

536
00:24:40.435 --> 00:24:42.698
They were weak.
didn't know how to negotiate.

537
00:24:42.872 --> 00:24:45.527
So now I'm their leader.

538
00:24:46.659 --> 00:24:49.226
Okay. And that means
you know where the shuttle is?

539
00:24:49.400 --> 00:24:51.751
I do. But what will you give me?

540
00:24:51.925 --> 00:24:53.100
What do you mean "give you"?

541
00:24:53.361 --> 00:24:54.681
Well. I need something in return.

542
00:24:54.841 --> 00:24:56.451
They were ready to just hand it over.

543
00:24:56.712 --> 00:24:58.322
Good! They should hand it over.

544
00:24:58.497 --> 00:24:59.759
I told them to up their game.

545
00:24:59.976 --> 00:25:02.196
So now I need to show them
how it's done.

546
00:25:04.241 --> 00:25:05.547
Give me your shirt.

547
00:25:05.721 --> 00:25:07.418
- My shirt? No.
- Give me your shirt.

548
00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:09.159
Give her your shirt.

549
00:25:09.333 --> 00:25:11.553
I'll say it has some kind of
deep Earth meaning.

550
00:25:11.727 --> 00:25:14.904
It does have a deep Earth
meaning. it's my favorite shirt.

551
00:25:16.558 --> 00:25:17.951
Uncalled for.

552
00:25:21.302 --> 00:25:22.956
- And now I'm chilly.
- Victory!

553
00:25:25.045 --> 00:25:26.786
<i>Okay. so. they found the shuttle</i>

554
00:25:26.960 --> 00:25:28.309
<i>hidden behind a billboard.</i>

555
00:25:28.483 --> 00:25:29.963
<i>Couldn't sell it because it's damaged</i>

556
00:25:30.137 --> 00:25:32.618
<i>and the operating chip is missing.</i>

557
00:25:36.447 --> 00:25:37.753
Can you fix this?

558
00:25:37.927 --> 00:25:39.494
We can use it to find the chip.

559
00:25:39.668 --> 00:25:40.713
Yeah.

560
00:25:40.887 --> 00:25:43.716
My tools are right... That is odd.

561
00:25:43.890 --> 00:25:46.196
Why are they out?

562
00:25:47.763 --> 00:25:49.765
No. I think it makes sense.

563
00:25:49.939 --> 00:25:51.379
You got the chip from the attendant.

564
00:25:51.419 --> 00:25:52.551
Which means you came here...

565
00:25:52.812 --> 00:25:54.509
- Wait.
- Tried to fix the shuttle

566
00:25:54.683 --> 00:25:56.313
because you are the king
of micromanaging.

567
00:25:56.337 --> 00:25:58.731
And were so drunk you broke it.
hid the shuttle

568
00:25:58.905 --> 00:26:00.360
to cover your mistake.
and totally screwed us over?

569
00:26:00.384 --> 00:26:02.212
<i>Scanning in progress.</i>

570
00:26:02.386 --> 00:26:04.345
<i>Shuttle Seven-E operating component</i>

571
00:26:04.519 --> 00:26:05.738
<i>is eight centimeters away.</i>

572
00:26:05.912 --> 00:26:07.696
It's in here.

573
00:26:07.870 --> 00:26:09.393
<i>20 centimeters away.</i>

574
00:26:09.568 --> 00:26:11.439
What did you do? Did you move it?

575
00:26:11.613 --> 00:26:13.528
I didn't touch anything.

576
00:26:13.702 --> 00:26:16.749
<i>11 centimeters away.</i>

577
00:26:19.882 --> 00:26:21.536
<i>0.3 centimeters away.</i>

578
00:26:21.710 --> 00:26:23.320
You gotta be kidding.

579
00:26:23.494 --> 00:26:26.236
Help me with this cast.

580
00:26:31.415 --> 00:26:33.156
The duotronic processing chip.

581
00:26:33.330 --> 00:26:35.942
You had it. Had it Have Had it.

582
00:26:36.116 --> 00:26:37.117
The whole time.

583
00:26:37.378 --> 00:26:38.814
There has to be an explanation.

584
00:26:39.119 --> 00:26:41.239
Yeah. I think the explanation
is that you're really...

585
00:26:54.438 --> 00:26:56.527
They stole my eyeballs!

586
00:26:56.702 --> 00:26:58.225
We've got bags on our heads.

587
00:27:00.749 --> 00:27:02.446
C-Can you reach my hands?

588
00:27:02.708 --> 00:27:04.361
Untie me.

589
00:27:10.541 --> 00:27:12.195
My eyeballs are still here.

590
00:27:12.369 --> 00:27:15.677
Here. here. move sideways.
maybe I can get you.

591
00:27:15.938 --> 00:27:17.418
Why aren't you yelling at me?

592
00:27:17.592 --> 00:27:19.115
Yelling just to yell?

593
00:27:19.289 --> 00:27:21.552
Like an "argh" kind of thing?

594
00:27:21.814 --> 00:27:24.120
Yelling because
I've been blaming you for

595
00:27:24.294 --> 00:27:26.054
losing the shuttle.
but apparently it was me.

596
00:27:26.122 --> 00:27:28.777
You just accepted that you did it.

597
00:27:28.951 --> 00:27:31.475
Get your foot out of my face.

598
00:27:31.650 --> 00:27:33.608
No. that I will not take the blame for.

599
00:27:33.782 --> 00:27:35.349
You moved your face to my foot.

600
00:27:41.660 --> 00:27:44.140
It's 'cause I grew up with six brothers.

601
00:27:44.314 --> 00:27:46.752
Bet your house smelled great.

602
00:27:47.013 --> 00:27:48.841
When things went wrong.
I got the blame.

603
00:27:49.015 --> 00:27:51.713
and they usually were my fault. so...

604
00:27:51.974 --> 00:27:54.281
Suppose I just assume
it's still that way now.

605
00:27:54.455 --> 00:27:56.326
I didn't know you had brothers.

606
00:27:56.500 --> 00:27:58.111
Hard to picture seven of you.

607
00:27:58.285 --> 00:27:59.590
Four adopted.

608
00:27:59.852 --> 00:28:01.767
Mom used to say that hearts are infinite.

609
00:28:01.941 --> 00:28:04.639
so we should make use of that space.

610
00:28:04.813 --> 00:28:07.468
Mine said something not too different.

611
00:28:10.340 --> 00:28:12.429
Okay. come on. Let's try again.

612
00:28:12.603 --> 00:28:13.953
Hang on! Hang on!

613
00:28:14.127 --> 00:28:15.868
I've almost got a grip.

614
00:28:16.042 --> 00:28:17.870
I used to get in trouble for blaming Beto

615
00:28:18.044 --> 00:28:19.764
for things that weren't entirely his fault.

616
00:28:20.002 --> 00:28:21.308
You mean your fault?

617
00:28:21.482 --> 00:28:23.266
Maybe all we needed to do
was compromise.

618
00:28:23.440 --> 00:28:25.268
Work together!

619
00:28:25.529 --> 00:28:27.140
I thought maybe
we'd say the same thing.

620
00:28:28.445 --> 00:28:31.535
- Dendru!
- Please...

621
00:28:31.710 --> 00:28:34.060
check your fisticuffs at the door.

622
00:28:34.234 --> 00:28:36.627
I only did what you both asked

623
00:28:36.802 --> 00:28:38.064
what you both begged me to do.

624
00:28:38.238 --> 00:28:40.588
Why would we want to be kidnapped?

625
00:28:40.762 --> 00:28:42.764
My journey is to do whatever I can

626
00:28:42.938 --> 00:28:45.114
to keep guests on their journey.

627
00:28:45.375 --> 00:28:47.377
My job is not to ask questions.

628
00:28:47.551 --> 00:28:49.379
Why would we want to be kidnapped?

629
00:28:49.684 --> 00:28:51.923
- My journey is to do whatever...
- I just asked that same question.

630
00:28:51.947 --> 00:28:53.079
I don't mind repeating it.

631
00:28:53.340 --> 00:28:55.037
What exactly did we ask you to do?

632
00:28:55.211 --> 00:28:57.387
"Dendru. no matter what.

633
00:28:57.561 --> 00:28:58.867
"keep us away from our shuttle.

634
00:28:59.041 --> 00:29:00.390
Tie us up if you have to."

635
00:29:00.564 --> 00:29:01.609
That does sound like me.

636
00:29:01.783 --> 00:29:03.524
And then we sealed the deal

637
00:29:03.698 --> 00:29:06.092
with what you called "big-up high-fives."

638
00:29:06.353 --> 00:29:07.658
Those are fun.

639
00:29:07.833 --> 00:29:09.312
Yes!

640
00:29:09.486 --> 00:29:11.358
Yeah. I'm gonna need more than that.

641
00:29:11.532 --> 00:29:14.840
No. it's okay. we have the chip.
we have the shuttle.

642
00:29:15.101 --> 00:29:16.581
We can go find the captain and leave.

643
00:29:16.667 --> 00:29:18.297
- Like. we did it.
- But we're missing something!

644
00:29:18.321 --> 00:29:21.020
- Don't you see that?
- Still so angry.

645
00:29:21.194 --> 00:29:25.285
I hoped your journey
would help you with that.

646
00:29:25.459 --> 00:29:26.982
Wait. did you plan this?

647
00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:31.900
You purposely gave me
us that note to deliver?

648
00:29:32.074 --> 00:29:33.922
When the message came in.
it seemed like a good thing

649
00:29:33.946 --> 00:29:37.514
for you to focus on.
instead of your frustrations.

650
00:29:37.688 --> 00:29:38.907
This has been a terrible trip.

651
00:29:39.081 --> 00:29:40.430
You are a terrible puppet master.

652
00:29:40.604 --> 00:29:42.563
I used to be a lot like you.

653
00:29:42.737 --> 00:29:44.260
I doubt it. smiley.

654
00:29:44.434 --> 00:29:48.525
I'm sorry that my plan didn't work.

655
00:29:49.570 --> 00:29:51.877
Because I do know how it feels
to always be looking

656
00:29:52.051 --> 00:29:54.444
for something to be angry about.

657
00:29:54.618 --> 00:29:55.881
If you look hard enough.

658
00:29:56.142 --> 00:29:58.100
you'll always find
some reason to be mad.

659
00:29:59.362 --> 00:30:02.409
You just need to decide
if you're going to ignore it.

660
00:30:02.583 --> 00:30:07.066
or let it ruin your day. or... or perhaps.

661
00:30:07.240 --> 00:30:11.461
try to figure out what it is
you're really angry about.

662
00:30:14.508 --> 00:30:17.685
We should... we need to go.

663
00:30:17.946 --> 00:30:21.341
You may want to stop by
Room C on your way.

664
00:30:21.515 --> 00:30:23.212
Apparently. one of your crew mates

665
00:30:23.386 --> 00:30:24.823
is causing an issue.

666
00:30:33.962 --> 00:30:35.834
We have G-47.

667
00:30:36.008 --> 00:30:39.054
Bingo! Bingo. bingo. bingo!
In your face. Leoda!

668
00:30:39.228 --> 00:30:41.448
You might as well just
give me your firstborn

669
00:30:41.622 --> 00:30:43.469
- 'cause I am coming for it!
- Not who I expected.

670
00:30:43.493 --> 00:30:46.453
All right. I think you've had enough.

671
00:30:46.627 --> 00:30:49.282
She can't leave yet!
I've gotta win my money back.

672
00:30:49.456 --> 00:30:51.414
Not my fault you can't cut it. Cornelia!

673
00:30:51.588 --> 00:30:54.113
This has gone on long enough.

674
00:30:54.374 --> 00:30:58.769
Now we play by our rules.

675
00:30:58.944 --> 00:31:00.641
Show me what you got!

676
00:31:00.815 --> 00:31:02.034
No. let's not show anything.

677
00:31:02.208 --> 00:31:03.992
Let's just show leaving.

678
00:31:04.166 --> 00:31:08.431
Heard rumors something ugly's
going down in here.

679
00:31:08.605 --> 00:31:10.781
Fight club!

680
00:31:11.043 --> 00:31:13.219
We have to go. The captain is waiting.

681
00:31:13.393 --> 00:31:16.309
- We need you.
- Avenge me!

682
00:31:18.485 --> 00:31:23.490
B-1. We have B-1.

683
00:31:25.405 --> 00:31:29.844
Hey. We sure hope
you'll come visit us again soon.

684
00:31:30.018 --> 00:31:31.618
<i>Be sure you have all of your belongings.</i>

685
00:31:31.715 --> 00:31:35.981
<i>including anyone you came with.
and no one extra.</i>

686
00:31:36.242 --> 00:31:38.635
She'll stay afloat
long enough to get us home.

687
00:31:38.809 --> 00:31:40.333
After that...

688
00:31:40.507 --> 00:31:42.770
Okay. guys.

689
00:31:42.944 --> 00:31:44.641
No matter what. this has to go well.

690
00:31:44.815 --> 00:31:48.297
We are Starfleet officers.
and as of right now.

691
00:31:48.558 --> 00:31:49.820
we are back on duty.

692
00:31:50.169 --> 00:31:53.302
Even if the world is on fire.
no interruptions.

693
00:31:53.476 --> 00:31:55.043
There's too much at stake.

694
00:31:55.217 --> 00:31:58.481
A steak sounds really good
right now. doesn't it?

695
00:31:58.655 --> 00:32:00.179
- Yes. sir.
- Why is that?

696
00:32:00.353 --> 00:32:02.703
I don't think the atmospheric effects

697
00:32:02.877 --> 00:32:04.705
have left our system yet.

698
00:32:04.879 --> 00:32:07.229
Yeah. I kind of picked up on that.

699
00:32:07.403 --> 00:32:10.929
<i>I guess they said it
affects everyone differently.</i>

700
00:32:19.198 --> 00:32:20.677
It's so bright.

701
00:32:24.072 --> 00:32:25.769
Formal hello.

702
00:32:25.944 --> 00:32:27.336
I am Co'Rah.

703
00:32:27.597 --> 00:32:31.340
Formal hello. I'm USS Christopher Pike.

704
00:32:31.514 --> 00:32:32.820
Formal welcome.

705
00:32:33.038 --> 00:32:34.778
We were surprised you requested

706
00:32:34.953 --> 00:32:36.563
the talks be pulled forward.

707
00:32:36.737 --> 00:32:38.497
Though we appreciate
your dedication to the matter.

708
00:32:38.521 --> 00:32:41.524
I do not recall making this request.

709
00:32:41.698 --> 00:32:43.526
Such a you thing to do though.

710
00:32:43.787 --> 00:32:45.702
Is something amiss?

711
00:32:45.876 --> 00:32:48.401
You are making strange sounds.

712
00:32:48.575 --> 00:32:49.750
Me?

713
00:32:49.924 --> 00:32:52.883
Everything's peachy.

714
00:32:53.058 --> 00:32:55.669
Formal peachy.

715
00:33:07.986 --> 00:33:10.814
Er... why are you here?

716
00:33:11.946 --> 00:33:13.295
Came to fix the shuttle.

717
00:33:13.469 --> 00:33:15.123
Figured it's the least I could do.

718
00:33:15.297 --> 00:33:18.126
- You?
- Same.

719
00:33:20.128 --> 00:33:21.651
Thanks.

720
00:33:24.567 --> 00:33:26.743
I can't stop thinking. like.

721
00:33:26.917 --> 00:33:28.180
why would you and I together

722
00:33:28.354 --> 00:33:30.443
ask to be kept apart from the shuttle?

723
00:33:30.617 --> 00:33:32.271
Like. what were we even doing together?

724
00:33:32.445 --> 00:33:34.403
Good point.

725
00:33:36.318 --> 00:33:38.842
Remember earlier how I said
I used to blame Beto

726
00:33:39.104 --> 00:33:40.279
for things that weren't...

727
00:33:40.453 --> 00:33:41.758
fully his fault?

728
00:33:41.932 --> 00:33:43.238
Things that were your fault.

729
00:33:43.499 --> 00:33:44.674
Let me get this out.

730
00:33:46.154 --> 00:33:48.678
The reason is that I was...

731
00:33:48.939 --> 00:33:50.245
maybe jealous.

732
00:33:50.419 --> 00:33:53.509
He's a natural at everything.

733
00:33:53.683 --> 00:33:56.121
and I think I wanted to see
something be hard

734
00:33:56.295 --> 00:33:59.080
for someone besides me.

735
00:34:00.734 --> 00:34:02.475
You know I failed Impulse Mechanics?

736
00:34:02.649 --> 00:34:04.825
The intro course.

737
00:34:04.999 --> 00:34:07.610
I joined the Academy to be an engineer.

738
00:34:07.784 --> 00:34:11.223
but I never had the head
for intermix chambers. I guess.

739
00:34:11.397 --> 00:34:14.487
Luckily. I had a head for flying.

740
00:34:14.661 --> 00:34:17.881
Well. intermix chambers are overrated.

741
00:34:18.056 --> 00:34:20.275
I've been so angry at you lately.

742
00:34:20.449 --> 00:34:22.538
and it's not even you I'm mad at.

743
00:34:22.712 --> 00:34:27.065
It's just the idea of me
not being good enough.

744
00:34:27.239 --> 00:34:29.676
When you pointed out
that my flying could be better.

745
00:34:29.850 --> 00:34:32.070
it just...

746
00:34:32.244 --> 00:34:34.333
set me off.

747
00:34:34.507 --> 00:34:37.379
Fun fact. I usually avoid the helm.

748
00:34:37.553 --> 00:34:39.153
That's why it was hard to picture myself

749
00:34:39.207 --> 00:34:40.207
stealing the shuttle.

750
00:34:40.295 --> 00:34:43.168
I once crashed one.

751
00:34:43.342 --> 00:34:44.865
Well. actually seven.

752
00:34:45.039 --> 00:34:47.781
It was during my only piloting class.

753
00:34:49.130 --> 00:34:51.350
I couldn't cut it.

754
00:34:51.524 --> 00:34:55.354
and maybe I'm a bit...

755
00:34:55.528 --> 00:34:59.097
envious of anyone who did.

756
00:34:59.271 --> 00:35:01.664
It's easy to get mad
at people who seem...

757
00:35:01.838 --> 00:35:03.753
better than me.

758
00:35:03.927 --> 00:35:07.105
Blame them for things.
try to bring them down a peg.

759
00:35:07.279 --> 00:35:09.803
I guess like my brothers
did to me. you know?

760
00:35:10.064 --> 00:35:12.022
That's a lot of crashed shuttles.

761
00:35:12.197 --> 00:35:14.677
So. so many shuttles.

762
00:35:14.938 --> 00:35:17.680
Luckily. I had a head for engineering.

763
00:35:17.854 --> 00:35:20.857
- I guess we're...
- Not so different after all?

764
00:35:21.119 --> 00:35:23.164
I was going to say a couple of screw ups

765
00:35:23.425 --> 00:35:25.035
who found our callings. but yeah.

766
00:35:25.210 --> 00:35:27.037
Your thing. too.

767
00:35:28.126 --> 00:35:29.344
Yeah.

768
00:35:34.132 --> 00:35:36.656
What's this?

769
00:35:39.093 --> 00:35:40.877
Wait. what is this?

770
00:35:41.139 --> 00:35:42.749
- What is this? What is this?
- Sh...

771
00:35:43.793 --> 00:35:45.491
- Bomb.
- Bomb.

772
00:35:52.585 --> 00:35:55.240
This is... this is...

773
00:35:55.414 --> 00:35:57.503
Just... let's get it deactivated.

774
00:35:57.764 --> 00:35:59.287
This is reactive bomb casing.

775
00:35:59.461 --> 00:36:01.028
Is that exactly what it sounds like?

776
00:36:01.246 --> 00:36:05.293
If I move my hands.
it's going to well. you know.

777
00:36:05.467 --> 00:36:07.107
Any idea how big
that "you know" might be?

778
00:36:07.252 --> 00:36:10.516
Well. I'd rather not find out...

779
00:36:11.734 --> 00:36:13.432
I'm gonna go get help.

780
00:36:15.347 --> 00:36:17.566
You are joking me.

781
00:36:17.740 --> 00:36:21.875
Conflict is the infancy of progress.

782
00:36:22.049 --> 00:36:27.315
instrumental in creating a harmony.

783
00:36:27.489 --> 00:36:30.884
And though our differences in belief

784
00:36:31.058 --> 00:36:32.755
may seem immutable.

785
00:36:33.016 --> 00:36:37.412
sovereignties are dedicated
to negotiating conflicts

786
00:36:37.586 --> 00:36:40.981
through diplomacy. right?

787
00:36:41.242 --> 00:36:43.201
And this remains true

788
00:36:43.462 --> 00:36:46.726
this is for our alleyways...

789
00:36:46.900 --> 00:36:48.728
There is a bomb on board.

790
00:36:48.902 --> 00:36:50.947
Red alert.

791
00:36:51.121 --> 00:36:54.168
I don't know how big.

792
00:36:55.822 --> 00:36:56.562
Tell the captain.

793
00:36:56.736 --> 00:36:58.738
Important.

794
00:36:59.913 --> 00:37:01.088
Where did I put that?

795
00:37:01.349 --> 00:37:02.394
- Okay.
- Whether or not

796
00:37:02.568 --> 00:37:04.396
there is a democracy of voices

797
00:37:04.570 --> 00:37:07.747
which. frankly. I think there are.

798
00:37:10.140 --> 00:37:12.273
Lieutenant. I heard about the avocado.

799
00:37:12.447 --> 00:37:13.753
- What?
- The message you gave

800
00:37:14.014 --> 00:37:15.383
to Uhura.
which she passed down the line.

801
00:37:15.407 --> 00:37:17.104
"Palm. avocado bad. tell captain"?

802
00:37:17.278 --> 00:37:18.801
I should've known that wouldn't work.

803
00:37:19.062 --> 00:37:20.518
Using reverse human logic.
I deduced that you may have

804
00:37:20.542 --> 00:37:22.544
been referring to a bomb on board.

805
00:37:22.718 --> 00:37:25.678
Or just bad avocados.
Either way. I am here to help.

806
00:37:25.852 --> 00:37:28.550
I should warn you. however.
you are still a plant.

807
00:37:28.724 --> 00:37:30.465
Pull it together. man.

808
00:37:30.639 --> 00:37:32.815
We need you.

809
00:37:34.861 --> 00:37:37.429
Indeed. a highly
sensitive reactive casing.

810
00:37:37.603 --> 00:37:38.963
Was it attached to a power source?

811
00:37:38.995 --> 00:37:41.433
Self-powered. It was in there.

812
00:37:44.436 --> 00:37:46.133
One of our isolinear recording chips?

813
00:37:46.307 --> 00:37:48.266
- Has this been scanned?
- We didn't see it.

814
00:37:48.440 --> 00:37:51.399
Kinda dealing with other things.

815
00:37:54.446 --> 00:37:57.144
<i>Okay. this message is for - Us.</i>

816
00:37:57.318 --> 00:38:01.191
<i>Future us. Which means hey you.</i>

817
00:38:01.366 --> 00:38:03.411
<i>You guys are smart.</i>

818
00:38:03.585 --> 00:38:04.945
<i>You'll figure out what's going on.</i>

819
00:38:05.108 --> 00:38:06.762
<i>- They we...
- Right?</i>

820
00:38:06.936 --> 00:38:08.460
<i>Definitely will.</i>

821
00:38:08.721 --> 00:38:10.331
<i>We each came back to fix the shuttle!</i>

822
00:38:10.505 --> 00:38:12.159
<i>- Shut up. man. What?
- Just let me talk.</i>

823
00:38:12.333 --> 00:38:13.856
<i>Let me talk. let me talk.</i>

824
00:38:14.204 --> 00:38:16.206
<i>We found out someone
tampered with the shuttle.</i>

825
00:38:16.381 --> 00:38:17.643
<i>Shuttle's a funny word.</i>

826
00:38:17.817 --> 00:38:19.166
<i>"Shuttle." Yeah. yeah.</i>

827
00:38:19.340 --> 00:38:20.776
<i>Someone messed with the shuttle.</i>

828
00:38:22.169 --> 00:38:23.518
<i>Maybe to ruin the peace talks?</i>

829
00:38:23.692 --> 00:38:25.172
<i>Maybe to be a big jerk.</i>

830
00:38:25.346 --> 00:38:27.087
<i>We don't know what they did yet.</i>

831
00:38:27.305 --> 00:38:29.568
<i>But we're going to hide the
"shushle" until we find Pike.</i>

832
00:38:29.742 --> 00:38:33.398
<i>just to make sure no one uses it
for. like. bad-guy reasons.</i>

833
00:38:33.572 --> 00:38:37.010
<i>I hid the chip in this fake cast.</i>

834
00:38:37.184 --> 00:38:39.534
<i>In case this place makes us
forget what we're doing.</i>

835
00:38:39.708 --> 00:38:41.406
<i>Future us. no matter what.</i>

836
00:38:41.623 --> 00:38:43.756
<i>do not bring the shuttle back
to the</i> Enterprise

837
00:38:43.930 --> 00:38:46.976
<i>until we well. you figure this out.</i>

838
00:38:47.150 --> 00:38:49.327
<i>Let's go!</i>

839
00:38:50.719 --> 00:38:54.332
Yep. seems like past us could
have come up with a better plan.

840
00:38:54.506 --> 00:38:56.421
It is indeed not very logical.

841
00:38:56.595 --> 00:38:57.944
Okay. plant boy. just help.

842
00:38:59.728 --> 00:39:01.556
The bomb is comprised
of Quadrium particles

843
00:39:01.730 --> 00:39:03.558
rare. once native
to the Rodaxian system.

844
00:39:03.732 --> 00:39:07.867
combined with Varuvian and Nitrilin.

845
00:39:08.737 --> 00:39:11.218
The scale of the explosion
would be catastrophic.

846
00:39:13.263 --> 00:39:15.135
Can we transport it off?

847
00:39:15.309 --> 00:39:16.504
This combination is too volatile.

848
00:39:16.528 --> 00:39:17.548
That would initiate the bomb.

849
00:39:17.572 --> 00:39:18.791
- The captain?
- After I left

850
00:39:18.965 --> 00:39:20.072
the mess hall. he locked the room.

851
00:39:20.096 --> 00:39:21.576
Then I'll break the door down!

852
00:39:21.881 --> 00:39:23.293
- We have to do something.
- There is too little time.

853
00:39:23.317 --> 00:39:24.903
- Jettison the shuttle.
- That will not help.

854
00:39:24.927 --> 00:39:26.644
As soon as you let go.
the bomb will explode.

855
00:39:26.668 --> 00:39:28.211
- Yeah. I won't let go.
- You can't do that. You'll die.

856
00:39:28.235 --> 00:39:29.497
We have no choice.

857
00:39:30.368 --> 00:39:32.674
Enough talking. just get off
this shuttle and let me go.

858
00:39:32.848 --> 00:39:34.937
You can't fly it. Both
your hands are on that bomb.

859
00:39:35.111 --> 00:39:36.374
I'll work it out.

860
00:39:38.332 --> 00:39:40.378
I'll work it out.

861
00:39:40.552 --> 00:39:42.118
I'm going with you.

862
00:39:42.292 --> 00:39:45.121
Spock. leave.

863
00:39:45.295 --> 00:39:46.993
We're doing this.

864
00:39:48.211 --> 00:39:51.345
I will attempt to transport you
out at the moment of detonation.

865
00:39:51.519 --> 00:39:54.261
A zeptosecond before explosion.

866
00:40:03.575 --> 00:40:06.708
It would certainly be easier
with another set of hands.

867
00:40:06.969 --> 00:40:08.449
On it.

868
00:40:09.494 --> 00:40:11.515
It is worse than I thought.
I am still hallucinating.

869
00:40:11.539 --> 00:40:14.063
We'll deal with that later.
I got the gist. but brief me.

870
00:40:14.237 --> 00:40:16.022
If only you were real.
I could use assistance

871
00:40:16.196 --> 00:40:17.589
- now more than ever.
- Spock

872
00:40:17.850 --> 00:40:21.723
I must concentrate.
Hallucination. begone.

873
00:40:25.292 --> 00:40:27.337
Was that imaginary?

874
00:40:27.512 --> 00:40:29.339
No. because it hurt. Didn't it?

875
00:40:30.210 --> 00:40:32.647
- You want another?
- I do not.

876
00:40:32.821 --> 00:40:33.953
Good.

877
00:40:34.388 --> 00:40:36.651
Now let's save this ship. and our friends.

878
00:40:36.825 --> 00:40:38.436
Recalibrate emitter array to compensate

879
00:40:38.697 --> 00:40:42.091
for Quadrium radiation variables
in bio filter assembly.

880
00:40:42.265 --> 00:40:44.442
Got it.

881
00:40:51.753 --> 00:40:53.102
I think it's happening.

882
00:40:53.276 --> 00:40:56.802
It's getting hotter. Very hot.

883
00:40:56.976 --> 00:40:59.848
Ortegas to Spock. This is it.

884
00:41:03.548 --> 00:41:04.723
Scotty.

885
00:41:04.897 --> 00:41:07.987
It's okay. I'm...

886
00:41:08.161 --> 00:41:10.206
I think we would have been friends.

887
00:41:10.380 --> 00:41:12.731
I think we already are.

888
00:41:23.263 --> 00:41:24.307
Formal I'm sorry.

889
00:41:24.482 --> 00:41:27.136
That was an insulting affront

890
00:41:27.397 --> 00:41:29.269
to our formal cultural traditions.

891
00:41:29.530 --> 00:41:31.401
history. and every principle

892
00:41:31.576 --> 00:41:34.013
these negotiations stand.

893
00:41:43.762 --> 00:41:45.067
Wow.

894
00:41:57.645 --> 00:41:59.604
- Are we...
- The afterlife

895
00:41:59.778 --> 00:42:02.041
looks surprisingly like the <i>Enterprise.</i>

896
00:42:02.215 --> 00:42:04.434
I think we're alive.

897
00:42:04.609 --> 00:42:06.219
You are indeed alive.

898
00:42:08.264 --> 00:42:10.876
- We're alive!
- We're alive!

899
00:42:21.060 --> 00:42:23.715
The Ancient Rodaxian
Formal Rite of Peace

900
00:42:23.889 --> 00:42:25.209
has not been seen in generations.

901
00:42:25.325 --> 00:42:28.110
The danger and expense and effort

902
00:42:28.284 --> 00:42:31.026
you must have put
into obtaining Quadrium.

903
00:42:31.200 --> 00:42:35.857
and invoking this
you've deeply honored us today.

904
00:42:36.858 --> 00:42:38.860
Let the peace talks now begin.

905
00:42:39.121 --> 00:42:42.472
In hopes of leaving as one planet.

906
00:42:43.822 --> 00:42:45.606
- You guys.
- All right.

907
00:42:45.780 --> 00:42:47.652
Bring it in.

908
00:42:47.826 --> 00:42:49.958
I think I'm sobering up. Did we really just

909
00:42:50.132 --> 00:42:51.132
come that close to dying?

910
00:42:51.351 --> 00:42:53.005
That was really. really close.

911
00:42:53.179 --> 00:42:55.529
I was holding on to the bomb!

912
00:42:55.703 --> 00:42:58.924
This really. really hurts now!

913
00:42:59.185 --> 00:43:00.839
Just okay. just.

914
00:43:01.013 --> 00:43:02.536
My God.

915
00:43:02.710 --> 00:43:04.277
Don't look at it.

916
00:43:04.625 --> 00:43:06.625
How can I not look at
it? It's looking right at me!

917
00:43:08.934 --> 00:43:10.892
Before you fade away. I must tell you.

918
00:43:11.153 --> 00:43:13.460
I have enjoyed our time together.

919
00:43:13.634 --> 00:43:15.549
Even though it was definitely not...

920
00:43:15.810 --> 00:43:17.159
We're going to sickbay!

921
00:43:17.333 --> 00:43:18.813
Hey. Kirk.

922
00:43:20.032 --> 00:43:21.642
- It's a paper cut.
- No. it's not!

923
00:43:21.816 --> 00:43:25.254
Real.

924
00:43:26.081 --> 00:43:27.169
They saw you.

925
00:43:27.343 --> 00:43:30.129
Spock. I'm not gonna fade away.

926
00:43:30.303 --> 00:43:33.741
I mean. at some point I'll leave
to go back to my ship.

927
00:43:33.915 --> 00:43:35.482
but you're not imagining me.

928
00:43:35.656 --> 00:43:37.310
Then why would you be here?

929
00:43:37.571 --> 00:43:39.747
Well. I was on vacation on Cesnar.

930
00:43:39.921 --> 00:43:41.227
I'm glad I ran into you.

931
00:43:41.488 --> 00:43:43.229
It was nice to get to know you better.

932
00:43:43.403 --> 00:43:46.014
A mind meld only takes you so far.

933
00:43:46.188 --> 00:43:49.104
I told you everything.

934
00:43:50.497 --> 00:43:53.108
- Everything.
- You sure did.

935
00:43:53.282 --> 00:43:58.287
And those many.
many secrets are safe with me.

936
00:44:00.333 --> 00:44:01.987
Are you going to hug me again?

937
00:44:02.161 --> 00:44:04.337
Do you want me to?

938
00:44:04.511 --> 00:44:05.773
Okay. highlights.

939
00:44:06.034 --> 00:44:07.949
- You two...
- I don't want to hear it.

940
00:44:08.123 --> 00:44:10.038
Running into that costume party

941
00:44:10.212 --> 00:44:11.518
trying to talk to Pike

942
00:44:11.692 --> 00:44:13.372
and having to put on
those loaner costumes.

943
00:44:13.607 --> 00:44:16.305
I can't even think about how
many people wore that before me.

944
00:44:16.479 --> 00:44:18.612
Though that does explain
why I still smell it.

945
00:44:18.786 --> 00:44:21.136
- Gross. dude.
- Why we all still smell it.

946
00:44:21.397 --> 00:44:23.037
I will forever regret missing your party.

947
00:44:23.095 --> 00:44:24.270
Appropriate.

948
00:44:24.531 --> 00:44:25.793
We weren't invited.

949
00:44:26.011 --> 00:44:27.249
I still don't understand
what happened though.

950
00:44:27.273 --> 00:44:30.189
Spock said I "got the dragon."

951
00:44:30.363 --> 00:44:31.973
- The "dragon bomb."
- What?

952
00:44:32.234 --> 00:44:34.584
You knocked over something
Dendru called a "dragon bomb."

953
00:44:34.759 --> 00:44:37.283
It was supposed to be
a relaxing airborne vapor.

954
00:44:37.457 --> 00:44:39.938
- enough for the whole club.
- But you two

955
00:44:40.112 --> 00:44:41.432
may have inhaled the whole thing.

956
00:44:41.591 --> 00:44:42.592
That explains a lot.

957
00:44:42.767 --> 00:44:44.769
- Good news.
- Hey!

958
00:44:44.943 --> 00:44:46.422
The saboteur has been apprehended.

959
00:44:46.596 --> 00:44:48.250
Some Rodaxian militant

960
00:44:48.468 --> 00:44:50.446
that would clearly do anything
to stop the negotiations.

961
00:44:50.470 --> 00:44:52.777
Including plotting to blow up
leaders from both factions.

962
00:44:52.951 --> 00:44:54.517
while they were aboard the <i>Enterprise.</i>

963
00:44:54.692 --> 00:44:57.172
Chris. you have something...

964
00:44:57.346 --> 00:44:59.392
Doc. could you remove these. please?

965
00:45:04.789 --> 00:45:07.139
- Hey. there he is!
- Excuse me.

966
00:45:07.313 --> 00:45:08.488
All right. nimble fingers.

967
00:45:08.662 --> 00:45:09.662
Doctor.

968
00:45:09.750 --> 00:45:11.012
Wow!

969
00:45:11.186 --> 00:45:14.712
Yes. to help with the decision-making.

970
00:45:14.886 --> 00:45:17.105
Thank you. sir.

971
00:45:17.366 --> 00:45:19.717
Hey. what do you guys think
about maybe making this. like.

972
00:45:19.978 --> 00:45:21.849
like an annual crew trip?

973
00:45:22.023 --> 00:45:23.808
Yeah. if I can wear that dress again.

974
00:45:23.982 --> 00:45:25.157
- Come on. dude.
- Yeah.

975
00:45:25.418 --> 00:45:27.246
Does anyone want to see my tattoo?

976
00:45:27.420 --> 00:45:28.421
No.

977
00:45:28.595 --> 00:45:30.162
There we go!

978
00:45:30.336 --> 00:45:32.817
<i>Personal log. supplemental.</i>

979
00:45:32.991 --> 00:45:35.341
<i>We're back in the rocky area of space...</i>

980
00:45:37.082 --> 00:45:38.997
<i>which. as any pilot knows...</i>

981
00:45:40.302 --> 00:45:43.262
<i>sometimes you gotta
push your way forward.</i>

982
00:45:43.436 --> 00:45:45.481
<i>But sometimes</i>

983
00:45:45.655 --> 00:45:48.354
<i>you just need to get out of your own way.</i>

984
00:45:50.225 --> 00:45:53.185
Don't tell me this is all from
pushing the thrusters a little?

985
00:45:53.359 --> 00:45:55.143
I wasn't exaggerating.

986
00:45:55.317 --> 00:45:58.277
Here. hand me that cell.

987
00:46:00.496 --> 00:46:03.412
Guess I could ease into it a little more.

988
00:46:03.586 --> 00:46:06.111
instead of punching.

989
00:46:07.808 --> 00:46:09.288
Come on.

990
00:46:09.462 --> 00:46:11.092
I'm actually working
to reroute the way power

991
00:46:11.116 --> 00:46:12.378
is distributed through the.

992
00:46:12.552 --> 00:46:16.164
Your favorite. the intermix chamber.

993
00:46:16.338 --> 00:46:18.776
That might allow you
a wee bit more push.

994
00:46:18.950 --> 00:46:20.255
But. you know. just a wee bit.

995
00:46:20.429 --> 00:46:21.996
Okay?

996
00:46:22.910 --> 00:46:24.520
Deal.

997
00:46:24.694 --> 00:46:25.870
And I won't let you down.

998
00:46:26.044 --> 00:46:27.480
I know you won't.

999
00:46:45.063 --> 00:46:46.503
We should have started it like this.

1000
00:46:46.542 --> 00:46:47.282
- Let's do it again.
- Let's do it again.

1001
00:46:47.456 --> 00:46:48.806
Let's do it again.

1002
00:47:35.591 --> 00:47:36.591
Perfect.

1003
00:47:36.810 --> 00:47:38.768
Nailed it.

1004
00:47:42.468 --> 00:47:44.252
Captioning sponsored by.

1005
